$ nexoctl cors get mem/site
`mem/site` has no CORS configuration.

$ nexoctl cors set mem/site cors.json
CORS configuration of `mem/site` set (1 rule).

$ nexoctl cors get mem/site
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "web",
      "allowedOrigins": [
        "https://app.example.com"
      ],
      "allowedMethods": [
        "GET",
        "PUT"
      ],
      "maxAgeSeconds": 600
    }
  ]
}

$ nexoctl cors get --xml mem/site
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CORSConfiguration xmlns="http://s3.amazonaws.com/doc/2006-03-01/">
  <CORSRule>
    <ID>web</ID>
    <AllowedOrigin>https://app.example.com</AllowedOrigin>
    <AllowedMethod>GET</AllowedMethod>
    <AllowedMethod>PUT</AllowedMethod>
    <MaxAgeSeconds>600</MaxAgeSeconds>
  </CORSRule>
</CORSConfiguration>

$ nexoctl cors set mem/site aws.json
CORS configuration of `mem/site` set (1 rule).

$ nexoctl cors get --json mem/site
{"status":"success","target":"mem/site","bucket":"site","rules":[{"allowedOrigins":["*"],"allowedMethods":["GET"],"exposeHeaders":["ETag"]}]}

$ nexoctl cors set mem/site cors.xml
CORS configuration of `mem/site` set (1 rule).

$ nexoctl cors get mem/site
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "allowedOrigins": [
        "https://*.example.com"
      ],
      "allowedMethods": [
        "HEAD"
      ],
      "allowedHeaders": [
        "*"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

$ nexoctl cors set mem/site bad.json
! nexoctl: error: invalid CORS configuration: Found unsupported HTTP method in CORS config. Unsupported method is PATCH: invalid argument
! Run 'nexoctl cors set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl cors set mem/site missing.json
! nexoctl: error: open missing.json: no such file or directory
[exit 3]

$ nexoctl cors rm mem/site
Removed the CORS configuration of `mem/site`.

$ nexoctl cors get mem/site
`mem/site` has no CORS configuration.

